{"schema":"Open Geotour","version":0.8300000000000001,"id":"Cherokee","agent":"cherokee editor","attribution":"c.2022 Museum of the Cherokee Indian","author":"D Jacobson","url":null,"theme":null,"lat":35.59455421995878,"lng":-83.40935544819946,"zoom":14,"pins":[{"id":"start","lat":35.58831379806755,"lng":-83.40558944276012,"zones":[{"radius":286.28437569062635,"sweep":0.07858321062602147,"id":"webb_overlook_-_100_yds","slice":0.8275416364493371,"speak":"Prepare to turn left to view Kuwahi Mountain from the Webb Overlook just ahead."},{"id":"Zone_1","radius":816.4051418295974,"slice":0.9199820362769866,"sweep":0.045928771400192615,"speak":"The tour begins by viewing Kuwahi Mountain from the Webb Overlook about a quarter mile away on your left"},{"id":"Zone_2","radius":1143.6036866216289,"slice":0.3697549479004852,"sweep":0.04011862097832609,"speak":"The tour begins by viewing Mount Kuwahi from the Webb Overlook about a half mile away on your right."},{"id":"Zone_3","radius":10959.228870163719,"slice":0.39610483795234314,"sweep":0.037714632289076205,"speak":"We start our tour by viewing Kuwahi Mountain from the Webb Overlook, in North Carolina, about fifteen minutes away."},{"id":"Zone_4","radius":13556.313320659216,"slice":0.8780859165922299,"sweep":0.03399829796233549,"speak":"Our tour starts with a view of Mount Kuwahi from the Webb Overlook, about fifteen minutes up the mountain from here."},{"id":"Zone_5","radius":300,"speak":"Prepare to pull off on the right at the Webb Overlook just ahead.","slice":0.3300567107524729,"sweep":0.039021606816681875},{"id":"Zone_6","radius":79.57240649379592,"speak":"Pull off now into the Overlook to start the tour with a view of Kuwahi Mountain.","slice":-0.13709636657379282,"sweep":0.3839684757268689},{"id":"Leaving_Webb_Overlook","radius":46.53402511368956,"speak":"Leave the overlook and turn right to follow our tour down the mountain.","exit":true,"slice":0.3843593431489994,"sweep":0.9848286747183517,"next":"webb_overlook"},{"id":"Zone_8","radius":300,"slice":0.31615048156308756,"sweep":0.061162307082949924,"exit":true,"speak":"Whoops. It looks like you are going the wrong way. To follow our tour, find a safe place to turn around and drive down the mountain. If you have already viewed Mount Kuwahi from the overlook, drive past it now."},{"id":"Zone_9","radius":13163.107145949245,"slice":0.8766621481903666,"sweep":0.04127695476306767,"speak":"This is a GPS-guided driving tour of the Cherokee homelands. It is a two-hour tour, but it usually lasts longer. On the tour, you will drive sixty miles through mountains and coves. All roads are paved, but some are narrow with tight curves. The tour is not appropriate for large vehicles like motorhomes. Remember that, as always, you are responsible for the safety of your own vehicle. This tour is based on your geolocation. It is not timed. Go at your own speed. Stop and get out at any of our six major destinations or anyplace else. The tour will wait for you. It will guide you through towns and countryside. Please respect the community. You are their guest. This is voice of your navigator. I provide driving directions, but mostly you will listen to the natural voices of tribal storytellers who share with you eight classic Cherokee stories and dozens of scenes from their long history in this land. Enjoy your tour."}]},{"id":"first_fire_intro","lat":35.599892608056436,"lng":-83.4130028525119,"zones":[{"radius":348.5104851288486,"sweep":0.29175285409605134,"audio":"guide/first-fire.mp3","id":"first_fire","slice":0.663007644576595,"next":"first_fire"}]},{"id":"how_to_follow_directions_intro","lat":35.58885224831564,"lng":-83.36839176426992,"zones":[{"radius":202.1970656766013,"audio":"guide/directions.mp3","id":"how_to_follow_directions","next":"how_to_folllow_directions","slice":0.20190092178342434,"sweep":0.5774935966829182}]},{"id":"kuwahi_intro","lat":35.589002062758496,"lng":-83.39776542475275,"zones":[{"radius":191.34144535287186,"sweep":0.48336984258349314,"audio":"guide/kawahi.mp3","id":"kuwahi_1","slice":0.5393657547011605,"next":"kuwahi_outro"}]},{"id":"selu_and_kanate_intro","lat":35.436717046664796,"lng":-83.36988791906764,"zones":[{"radius":99.64598630880924,"audio":"guide/selu-kanati.mp3","id":"selu_and_kanate","slice":0.4754607585968174,"sweep":0.266733772515824,"next":"left_under_bridge"}]},{"id":"ballgame_of_birds_and_animals","lat":35.46671555271686,"lng":-83.3541909325677,"zones":[{"radius":332,"sweep":0.34772050314251546,"audio":"story/ballgame-of-birds-and-animals.mp3","id":"ballgame_of_birds_and_animals","slice":-0.05343189115496788,"next":"straight_past_bridge_0"}]},{"id":"first_fire","lat":35.599648285148085,"lng":-83.40748733288639,"zones":[{"radius":487.29532659498807,"sweep":0.14643932932600714,"audio":"story/first-fire-story.mp3","id":"first_fire","slice":0.37131469271533185,"next":"how_to_follow_directions_intro"}]},{"id":"how_to_folllow_directions","lat":35.58173812869682,"lng":-83.35137633386691,"zones":[{"radius":214.6312985818314,"audio":"story/how-to-follow-directions.mp3","id":"how_to_follow_directions","slice":0.0013482707403445898,"sweep":0.7585967287474038,"next":"Ranger_Station"}]},{"id":"kanati","lat":35.438456417120854,"lng":-83.35528417702807,"zones":[{"radius":59.92152274742658,"audio":"story/kanati.mp3","id":"kanati","slice":0.287122143205102,"sweep":0.45060095509634734,"next":"bear_left"}]},{"id":"selu","lat":35.44417980251836,"lng":-83.29877945743323,"zones":[{"radius":231,"audio":"story/selu.mp3","id":"selu","slice":0.40383210888518484,"sweep":0.33350918617594194,"next":"right_at_y"}]},{"id":"spear_finger","lat":35.512403240049835,"lng":-83.15883519121465,"zones":[{"radius":1109.4805989051176,"sweep":0.16982437168944411,"audio":"story/spearfinger.mp3","id":"spearfinger","slice":0.7175311482162876,"next":"thomas_divide_overlook"}]},{"id":"kituwah_mound","lat":35.43735482721607,"lng":-83.39921236156898,"zones":[{"radius":461.0020446503608,"id":"zone_00","audio":"guide/kituwah.mp3","slice":0.3950158989224874,"sweep":0.07480554844843251},{"id":"Zone_1","radius":504.4922195582805,"speak":"Turn left on Eela Road","slice":0.41806027879736496,"sweep":0.027890954179956018,"exit":true}]},{"id":"socco_falls","lat":35.492784497500196,"lng":-83.16964566795265,"zones":[{"radius":46.82654953451806,"sweep":0.19712658429299793,"speak":"Pull off the road and enjoy the Falls.","id":"zone_00","slice":0.3724757337946517},{"id":"Zone_1","radius":351.96968994697045,"slice":0.48086085523589256,"sweep":0.0802000533222995,"speak":"We are approaching Soco Falls. Be prepared to pull over to view the Falls before we continue our climb up Soco Gap."},{"id":"Zone_2","radius":128.91094817676594,"slice":0.3841182337337817,"sweep":0.21547517938863528,"speak":"The Falls are ahead in yiour righ. The parking area is small and unpaved and unmarked. Be very careful."},{"id":"Zone_3","radius":34.72710636343893,"audio":"guide/soco-falls.mp3"},{"id":"Zone_4","radius":30,"exit":true,"speak":"Be careful as you get back on the road and head further up the mountain.","slice":0.05024198518786388,"sweep":0.5366096975319978,"next":"pass"}]},{"id":"museum_of_the_cherokee","lat":35.4846219725705,"lng":-83.31650888280903,"zones":[{"radius":140.98413849876354,"sweep":0.0696575283069955,"speak":"The Museum is on the corner across the street on your left. You can pull off the road into the parking lot.","id":"zone_00","slice":0.04193628979922287},{"id":"Zone_1","radius":94.34563361394055,"speak":"enter the parking lot.","slice":-0.01874085187238861,"sweep":0.325589310609866},{"id":"Zone_2","radius":78.34978984681698,"audio":"guide/museum.mp3","next":"END"},{"id":"Zone_3","radius":364.5586169529023,"speak":"Prepare to stop at the Museum of the Cherokee Indian.","slice":0.13899968516856326,"sweep":0.08455445663576416},{"id":"Zone_4","radius":240.8721390548095,"speak":"The museum is the last stop on our tour. It is up ahead on our right, where you see the huge carving of Sequoya.","slic